coder › Done on branch `fix/csv-formula-injection` (2 commits).

What changed:
- `src/csv.ts`: `field()` now branches on type. `number` cells are written plainly via `String(cell)` (so `-2.5` stays `-2.5`). `string` cells starting with `=`, `+`, `-`, `@`, `\t`, or `\r` are written as `"'<text>"` (single-quote prefix, whole field double-quoted, inner `"` doubled). All other strings keep the existing rule: quote only if containing `,`, `"`, or `\n`, doubling inner `"`.
- `src/csv.test.ts`: kept the original comma test, added tests for `=HYPERLINK(...)` with embedded quotes, for `+`/`-`/`@`/tab/CR prefixes, for plain negative/positive numbers, and for quote/newline/plain quoting.

